            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0501" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-13T18:00:00+08:00">December 13, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—9:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. I have just received following message from American Consul, Shanghai: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 13th. Japanese Ambassador has requested me to transmit the
                            following message to you: <quote rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘I have to express my most profound regrets over the extremely
                                    unfortunate incident that has happened to the U. S. S. <hi
                                        rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> involving the members of your
                                    Embassy staff and your citizens as well as the officers and crew
                                    of the ship’.”</p>
                            </quote></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I am making following reply: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Please communicate following to Japanese Ambassador: <quote
                                rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘I thank you for your message. Word from Mr. Atcheson this
                                    afternoon reported survivors in Hohsien in danger presumably
                                    from attacking Japanese forces. H. M. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                                        >Bee</hi> now off Hohsien may have difficulty making contact
                                    with survivors. I hope you will do what you can to facilitate
                                    errand of H. M. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Bee</hi> which has
                                    gone to the rescue’.”</p>
                            </quote></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
